          "text": "The pattern is consistent with an **O3-layered, half-lithiated nickel oxide**, Li\\(_{0.5}\\)NiO\\(_2\\) = LiNi\\(_2\\)O\\(_4\\), rather than a cubic spinel. It indexes on a slightly distorted triclinic cell in **\\(P\\bar1\\)**. Diagnostic assignments include 001 at 18.22\u00b0, 200 at 38.66\u00b0, 20\u22122 at 44.40\u00b0, 201 at 48.44\u00b0, 202 near 63.49\u00b0, and 020 near 65.61\u00b0. The splitting around 43\u201345\u00b0 rules out the higher-symmetry monoclinic parent as an exact description.\n\nLi and oxygen coordinates are less strongly constrained than the Ni framework by Cu X-ray data, so the oxygen positions below are a chemically restrained layered-model solution.\n\n```cif\ndata_LiNi2O4_layered_P-1\n_audit_creation_method            'Powder XRD indexing and restrained structure solution'\n_chemical_name_common             'half-lithiated layered nickel oxide'\n_chemical_formula_structural      'LiNi2O4'\n_chemical_formula_sum             'Li1 Ni2 O4'\n_chemical_formula_weight          188.32\n_cell_formula_units_Z             1\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt         'P -1'\n_space_group_IT_number            2\n\n_cell_length_a                    4.9164\n_cell_length_b                    2.8452\n_cell_length_c                    5.1348\n_cell_angle_alpha                 90.23\n_cell_angle_beta                  108.63\n_cell_angle_gamma                 92.19\n_cell_volume                      68.00\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type            'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength      1.5406\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-x,-y,-z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\nLi1  Li  1  a  0.0000  0.0000  0.0000  1.0\nNi1  Ni  1  f  0.5000  0.0000  0.5000  1.0\nNi2  Ni  1  g  0.0000  0.5000  0.5000  1.0\nO1   O   2  i  0.2400  0.0000  0.7200  1.0\nO2   O   2  i  0.7400  0.5000  0.7200  1.0\n```\n\nThe structure is a Li-vacancy-ordered derivative of rhombohedral layered LiNiO\\(_2\\), with two crystallographically distinct Ni sites and one occupied Li site per LiNi\\(_2\\)O\\(_4\\) cell. A pseudo-monoclinic \\(P2/m\\) model is metrically close, but it does not account for the observed reflection splitting as well as the triclinic model.",
